--- body ---
## Context

Author, 2026-09-23: "the test should not block on that." A rung-3 run of the
0816 branch (work dir on the `/tmp` tmpfs, 7,8 GiB free) sat for its whole
index timeout while the sitter refused admission — `low-disk`, then
`cpu-busy` — retrying every 10 min. Neither `bench/sitter_smoke_test.py` nor
`bench/sitter_menagerie_test.py` knows the blocked phases exist: they wait on
completion, so a refusal reads as a timeout, and a timeout reads as a sitter
failure. A refusal is the sitter working as designed on a host that cannot
run the test.

## Actions

1. Preflight, before install: free space at the work directory against the
   sitter's disk floor plus a margin, and load against the core count. Refuse
   to start with a named reason ("work dir on <fs>: 7,8 GiB free, sitter needs
   8 GiB") rather than launch a run that cannot proceed. Read the floor from
   the plugin source or its exposed state, never a second literal.
2. During a run, every wait on the sitter also watches its phase: a phase in
   `SDT_BLOCKED_PHASES` ends the wait at once — after at most one forced
   retry (switch off/on) for a transient gate like `cpu-busy` — and the run
   exits NOT-RUN (environment), not FAIL, recording the gate and the
   admission readings (`describeSDTAdmission`'s fields) in the run record.
3. Keep the arena off the `/tmp` tmpfs by default. It is 12 GiB here, so
   against the sitter's 8 GiB floor a rung arena on `/tmp` works only while
   everything else on it stays under 4 GiB; on 2026-09-23 the 0816 lane's own
   ~20 kept run directories (1,3 GiB) and other sessions' scratch took it past
   that. `bench/sitter_smoke_test.py` defaults `--work-dir` to a bare
   `tempfile.mkdtemp()` (`/tmp`); `bench/sitter_menagerie_test.py` requires one
   and the lanes pass their scratchpad, also on `/tmp`. Default both under the
   `$ACCEPTANCE_ARENA` layout (on `~/data`), whose retention (0720) bounds it.
4. Both drivers, through one shared helper; 0818 (clone rung) and 0821
   (whole-corpus waits) use the same helper when they land.
5. Scope widened by the author, 2026-09-24: the clone-rung driver
   `bench/sitter_clone_rung.py` (landed with 0818, PR #625) waits on the
   sitter too and gets the same treatment, so the one shared helper serves
   three drivers: `bench/sitter_smoke_test.py`,
   `bench/sitter_menagerie_test.py`, `bench/sitter_clone_rung.py`.

## Test

Red first, with a faked state stream: a `low-disk` phase with work pending
must end the wait within one poll and yield NOT-RUN naming the gate; a
completing stream must still PASS; a preflight with free space below the
floor must refuse before any Zotero launch.

## Exit criteria

- A refused run exits NOT-RUN within a poll or a forced retry, with gate and
  readings recorded, never at the index timeout.
- The preflight refuses a work directory below the disk floor.
- Neither driver's default arena is on the `/tmp` tmpfs.
- Unit tests above, red before and green after.

Related: 0823 (the dialog side of the same refusal); consumers 0818, 0821.
